<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταβρίθω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ]</span>, intr., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be heavily laden, weighed
			down</i> by a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄϊες μαλλοῖς καταβεβρίθασι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					234
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρπακες βραβύλοισι καταβρίθοντες ἔραζε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					7.146
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>weigh down, outweigh</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλβῳ μὲν πάντας κε καταβρίθοι
					βασιλῆας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					17.95
				</span></i>
			.</div>
